url: "https://osman209.github.io/odd-sieve-cell-system/"
abstract: >-
  Twelve papers, one overview and thirty-three verification scripts on the
  elementary sieve of the odd numbers, developed as a coordinate system
  of lines and cells. Papers 1 to 4 build the coordinates and the
  transport laws; papers 5 to 8 are the construction and what it decides
  about twin pairs; papers 9 to 11 derive the point at which it stops
  from inside the construction rather than quoting it, and measure how
  much of the difficulty the framework can localise before failing to
  cross it; paper 12 stands apart from the system and uses none of its
  objects. Statements that are only measured are labelled as such and
  listed together, and withdrawn results are kept rather than deleted.
  Paper 1 is independent of the rest and concerns no prime numbers. No
  progress toward the twin-prime conjecture is claimed, and no new
  bound. Thirty-three verification scripts regenerate every number printed, each
  exiting non-zero when its claim fails.
keywords:
